@startuml Concurrent Prod and Test Requests
actor "Request A\n(prod operator)" as A
actor "Request B\n(test operator)" as B
participant "AsyncLocalStorage" as ALS
participant "EnvRouter Proxy" as Proxy
participant "Prod DB" as ProdDB
participant "Test DB" as TestDB

A -> ALS: t1: storage.run({ userType: "operator" })
B -> ALS: t2: storage.run({ userType: "test_operator" })

A -> Proxy: t3: db.execute()
activate Proxy
Proxy -> ALS: isTestRequest() [context A]
ALS --> Proxy: false
Proxy -> ProdDB: execute()
deactivate Proxy

B -> Proxy: t4: db.execute()
activate Proxy
Proxy -> ALS: isTestRequest() [context B]
ALS --> Proxy: true
Proxy -> TestDB: execute()
deactivate Proxy

A -> Proxy: t5: db.execute()
activate Proxy
Proxy -> ALS: isTestRequest() [context A]
ALS --> Proxy: false
Proxy -> ProdDB: execute()
deactivate Proxy

note over Proxy: no shared mutable state -\nNode.js propagates ALS per async context tree,\nso request A is never polluted by request B
@enduml
